 (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\languages\\page.tsx:594:62\n  592 |         totalQuestions={TOTAL_Q}\n  593 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n> 594 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n      |                                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  595 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n  596 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n  597 |         autoLoad","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\languages\\page.tsx:595:20\n  593 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n  594 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n> 595 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n      |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  596 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n  597 |         autoLoad\n  598 |       />","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\languages\\page.tsx:596:39\n  594 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n  595 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n> 596 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n      |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  597 |         autoLoad\n  598 |       />\n  599 |       <div className=\"flex gap-3 mt-3\">","'correct' is assigned a value but never used.","Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Date.now` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\math\\page.tsx:170:28\n  168 |   const timerRef  = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | null>(null);\n  169 |   const advRef    = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);\n> 170 |   const startRef  = useRef(Date.now());\n      |                            ^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  171 |   const totalMsRef = useRef(0);\n  172 |   const correctRef = useRef(0);\n  173 |   const streakRef  = useRef(0);","Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\n\n`nextQ` is accessed before it is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\math\\page.tsx:215:43\n  213 |         const now = Date.now(); totalMsRef.current += now - startRef.current; startRef.current = now;\n  214 |         streakRef.current = 0; setStreak(0);\n> 215 |         advRef.current = setTimeout(() => nextQ(idx + 1), 900);\n      |                                           ^^^^^ `nextQ` accessed before it is declared\n  216 |       }\n  217 |     }, 100);\n  218 |     startRef.current = Date.now();\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\math\\page.tsx:183:3\n  181 |   };\n  182 |\n> 183 |   const nextQ = useCallback((idx: number) => {\n      |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 184 |     if (idx >= TOTAL_Q) {\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 185 |       // Done\n      …\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 218 |     startRef.current = Date.now();\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 219 |   }, [genQuestion, onFinish, subject]);\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `nextQ` is declared here\n  220 |\n  221 |   const handleAnswer = useCallback((choice: number) => {\n  222 |     if (selected !== null) return;",{"range":"6830","text":"6798"},"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\math\\page.tsx:278:22\n  276 |         correctAnswers={result.correct}\n  277 |         totalQuestions={TOTAL_Q}\n> 278 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n      |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  279 |         maxLevel={Math.max(...levels, 1)}\n  280 |         maxStreak={maxStreak}\n  281 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\math\\page.tsx:281:39\n  279 |         maxLevel={Math.max(...levels, 1)}\n  280 |         maxStreak={maxStreak}\n> 281 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n      |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  282 |         autoLoad\n  283 |       />\n  284 |       <div className=\"flex gap-2 mt-3\">","'_c' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\page.tsx:134:5\n  132 |   useEffect(() => {\n  133 |     fetchMeWithRetry(2, 100).then((me) => setUser(me)).catch(() => {});\n> 134 |     setIqData(getIQData());\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  135 |   }, []);\n  136 |\n  137 |   return (",["6831","6832"],"Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\n\n`nextQ` is accessed before it is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\nK:\\crispy-octo-doodle-77829d00d8261df34286efbaf5533562290f6fae\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\physics\\pa